{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on `50a673b7`: the production adapter of C4 is the replica\nalone.\n\n1. The adapter. The context comes from the matching member session,\n   the checked Replica and the pinned declaration. `standing` is\n   null, because no grant was read. The context holds no foreign\n   fact and no observation. An act that needs one of those inputs\n   gets its lacks. C4 adds no read and acquires no grant.\n2. This serves rule 3 of section 6. `judgeActBody` checks the\n   expected basis before it needs authority, so a stale draft gets\n   the determinate answer that its basis moved, and it returns\n   before a signature. An unchanged basis answers `unavailable`, and\n   the submit proceeds, as `16211297` item 4 says. Item 4's second\n   reader is not needed. Pin the order of those two checks with one\n   test in the judge's owner, so a later reorder fails there.\n3. The constructor port stays as the seam, with this one adapter.\n   C4 builds no second adapter.\n4. The witness stays in this repository. I withdraw the page\n   criterion of `16211297`: no page in this repository uses\n   `ScopeClient`, and the pinboard page lives in another repository.\n   Request `7555a333` puts that work outside C4. C4 is working when\n   its suite shows three things on the in-memory scope with a real\n   session and a real Replica: a stale draft of an `observed` act\n   returns before any signature with `now`, the same draft with an\n   unchanged basis submits and records, and the memory form and the\n   browser form of the stores give the same result. Use a definition\n   that this repository holds, and name it.\n5. Do not bind or change `dap-ui-sdk` under C4.\n6. Finish the producer analysis of the Lending pending state in the\n   audit. It holds no source.\n\nThe audit also shows a gap that C4 does not own. No read gives a\nmember's instance its present grants. So an exploration in a local\ninstance or in the agent host is `unavailable` for each act with an\nunchanged basis, and E2 and E3 cannot give the answers that section\n5.5 promises. I take that as a design question before E2 or E3\nstarts. File the full audit as one implementation note in the C4\nhead, and send me its path in your worktree now, so I can read the\nreads and the limits.\n\nOn `a31ea4cb`: one shared decoder over the E4 model, which refuses a\nmalformed history before any write, is right. No decision needed.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}